  "body": "## vulnerability details\n\nUnder PM mode, executeHedge() optimistically registers a supplied slot in the accountant immediately after enqueuing the HyperCore spot/perp actions. But HyperCore actions are asynchronous, and the 0x811 supplied slot may not exist yet when the accountant later reads it. Because the accountant intentionally performs strict reads on every registered slot, a single premature registration can cause totalBackingSigned() to revert, which in turn bricks surplus(), distributableSurplus(), settle(), and any workflow that depends on them.\n\n## Summary\n\n PM-mode auto-registration can poison the 0x811 supplied-slot registry before HyperCore actually activates the slot, which can brick totalBacking(), surplus(), and settle().\n\n## Root cause\n\nexecuteHedge() does two logically separate things:\n\n1. it sends the spot/perp actions to HyperCore\n2. it immediately calls notifyVaultSupply() when pmEnabled\n\nThat registration is treated by the accountant as a hard promise that the slot is live and readable. During backing reads, the accountant iterates every registered supplied asset and uses PrecompileReader.suppliedBalance() or suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(...). Those reads are fail-closed. If HyperCore has not actually activated the supplied slot yet, the read reverts.\n\nThe key problem is that the code assumes \"action submitted\" and \"0x811 slot live\" are equivalent states. They are not.\n## Broken invariants\n\n- README INV-1: backing becomes unreadable due to an internally created stale registration entry\n- README INV-7 / INV-9 pipeline liveness: settlement can no longer evaluate distributable surplus once total backing reverts\n- README area-of-concern #2: precompile read semantics and fail-closed behavior\n\n## Attack / failure path\n\n1. Governor enables PM mode and whitelists a hedge asset.\n2. Operator calls executeHedge().\n3. The spot leg is only enqueued on HyperCore, delayed, or partially/unfilled.\n4. executeHedge() still calls notifyVaultSupply() right away.\n5. The accountant now has a registered supplied slot for that token.\n6. Any later call to totalBackingSigned() attempts a strict 0x811 read for the registered token.\n7. If the slot is not actually active yet, the precompile read reverts.\n8. Accounting-dependent flows are bricked until operators manually repair state.\n\n\n\n## Why this is not a known issue\n\nThe README discusses strict 0x811 handling and trusted operators, but it does not disclose that the vault itself can create self-poisoning registry entries before the HyperCore state transition they are supposed to represent has happened.\n\n## Impact\nThis is a protocol liveness failure with direct economic consequences:\n\n- yield settlement can halt\n- surplus checks can halt\n- redemption and risk operations relying on backing observability can be delayed\n- the system can remain stuck until privileged intervention happens\n\nAlthough this does not directly steal funds, it can freeze critical accounting and settlement flows, which is a solid Medium.\n\n\n## Tool Used\nManual Review, Slither\n\n## Recommendation\nDo not register a supplied slot until the slot is provably live.\n\nSafer options:\n\n- register only after a successful explicit 0x811 read\n- separate \"pending PM slot\" from \"active PM slot\" in the accountant\n- or add an operator-controlled reconciliation path that can safely clear premature entries without bricking reads.\n\nIf strict fail-closed accounting is desired, the registration step must be equally strict about actual slot activation.",
  "proof_of_concept": "PoCs\nRun:\nforge test --match-path test/SoloFindingsPoC.t.sol -vvv\n\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport {C4Submission, _PoCMockPrecompile} from \"./c4/C4Submission.t.sol\";\nimport {MonetrixConfig} from \"../src/core/MonetrixConfig.sol\";\nimport {MonetrixVault} from \"../src/core/MonetrixVault.sol\";\nimport {ActionEncoder} from \"../src/core/ActionEncoder.sol\";\nimport {HyperCoreConstants} from \"../src/interfaces/HyperCoreConstants.sol\";\n\ncontract SoloFindingsPoC is C4Submission {\n    function _mockSpotUsdc(address account, uint64 l1Amount8dp) internal {\n        _PoCMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SPOT_BALANCE)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(account, uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)),\n            abi.encode(l1Amount8dp, uint64(0), uint64(0))\n        );\n    }\n\n\n    function test_M2_pmAutoRegistrationCanBrickAccountingBeforeHyperCoreActivatesSlot() public {\n        uint32 perpIndex = 4;\n        uint32 spotToken = 221;\n        uint32 spotPairAssetId = 10_151;\n\n        vm.startPrank(admin);\n        config.addTradeableAsset(\n            MonetrixConfig.TradeableAsset({\n                perpIndex: perpIndex,\n                spotIndex: spotToken,\n                spotPairAssetId: spotPairAssetId\n            })\n        );\n        vault.setPmEnabled(true);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // The hedge action only enqueues asynchronous HyperCore orders. If the\n        // spot leg does not fill yet, the 0x811 slot is still absent.\n        vm.mockCallRevert(\n            HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE,\n            abi.encode(address(vault), uint64(spotToken)),\n            \"slot not activated\"\n        );\n\n        ActionEncoder.HedgeParams memory params = ActionEncoder.HedgeParams({\n            spotAsset: spotPairAssetId,\n            perpAsset: perpIndex,\n            size: 1e8,\n            spotPrice: 1e8,\n            perpPrice: 1e8,\n            cloid: 0,\n            tif: 2,\n            spotReduceOnly: false,\n            perpReduceOnly: false\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(operator);\n        vault.executeHedge(1, params);\n\n        assertEq(accountant.vaultSuppliedLength(), 1, \"slot was registered optimistically\");\n\n        vm.expectRevert(bytes(\"PrecompileReader: supplied balance read failed\"));\n        accountant.totalBacking();\n    }\n}\n\n\n\nThe PoC mocks the 0x811 precompile to revert for the newly registered token, then shows:\n\n- `executeHedge()` still registers the slot\n- `accountant.totalBacking()` reverts with `PrecompileReader: supplied balance read failed`",
